{
  "$schema": "https://appflare.github.io/catalog/schema/v1.json",
  "slug": "wx2md",
  "name": "wx2md",
  "summary": "Turns WeChat Official Account articles, and any other web page, into clean Markdown or a readable HTML view: swap the article link's host for your Worker's, on Workers AI Markdown conversion.",
  "tagline": "Turn WeChat articles and web pages into Markdown",
  "features": [
    "Convert a WeChat article by changing its link to your own address",
    "Download converted articles as Markdown files",
    "Read converted articles in an HTML view",
    "Convert other web pages by providing their address"
  ],
  "homepage": "https://mp.084817.xyz",
  "repo": "loadchange/wx2md-worker",
  "license": "MIT",
  "categories": ["utilities", "ai"],
  // Edited help text (revision 2), field links (revision 3) and the formatting of
  // URLs in the notes (revision 4) came after this release was published:
  // revisions, no new build.
  // Added features (revision 6), no new build.
  "revision": 6,
  "authors": [{ "name": "Asa", "github": "loadchange" }],
  "maintainers": ["MendyLanda"],
  // Upstream publishes no tags; the pin is the head of main.
  "source": { "ref": "main", "sha": "3fa0184da7c8fe1f5315da82da7339389624d739" },
  "install": {
    "packageManager": "pnpm",
    "wranglerConfig": "wrangler.jsonc",
    "health": { "path": "/health" },
    // The wrangler config points R2_PUBLIC_URL at upstream's own image domain,
    // which an install cannot write to. Removing it leaves image rehosting off
    // until the admin sets the var below. No upstream pull request yet.
    "configPatch": { "vars": { "R2_PUBLIC_URL": null } }
  },
  // Workers AI's Markdown conversion of HTML is free, and the R2 bucket stays
  // empty until image rehosting is turned on.
  "plan": "free",
  "requires": ["workers-ai", "r2"],
  "vars": [
    {
      "name": "R2_PUBLIC_URL",
      "label": "Public image address",
      "help": "The public address of this install's R2 bucket (its r2.dev URL or a custom domain, without a trailing slash). When set, article images are copied to the bucket and linked from there, since WeChat blocks hotlinking. Leave empty to keep the original image links.",
      "link": {
        "label": "Open the dashboard",
        "url": "https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/r2/overview"
      },
      "default": "",
      "optional": true
    }
  ],
  "postInstall": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Replace `https://mp.weixin.qq.com` in an article link with `{{appUrl}}`, for example `{{appUrl}}/s/<article id>`. Use `/html/s/<article id>` for a readable page, add `?download=true` to download the Markdown, or convert any page with `{{appUrl}}/md?url=<address>`."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "To show article images, which WeChat does not serve to other sites: in the Cloudflare dashboard open R2, select the bucket `{{workerName}}-images-bucket`, turn on public access (r2.dev or a custom domain), and **add an object lifecycle rule that deletes objects after 1 day**, since the Worker never deletes the images it copies. Then set the public address in this app's settings."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "The Worker has no sign-in: anyone with its address can convert pages through it."
    }
  ]
}
